{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds","id":1498657,"title":"Teaching Gifts between Breeds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-03T03:58:14-08:00","id":1498657,"title":"Teaching Gifts between Breeds","content":"Does anyone have a super quick explanation for how teaching between breeds works?<br /> <br /> For instance, a Garou asks a rat spirit to teach them Danger Sense, a level 1 Tunnel Runner gift. The spirit refuses, naturally. The Garou *forces* them to, using a Gift or a Rite, or threats of destruction. What now?<br /> <br /> In another example, a Bastet tries to teach a Garou a Gift. What then?<br /> <br /> Does being in a mixed-breed Pack like the Ahadi help? Is it usually impossible? Are some gifts just beyond the Garou?<br /> <br /> Naturally some require anatomy they lack! And others the spirit world won't want them to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T05:01:47-08:00","id":1498659,"title":"","content":"AFAIK, there's not much in the way of limitations on learning Gifts, since in the end, they all spring from the teachings of spirits as a source.<br /> <br /> Should not be much harder than learning a gift not from one's auspice, breed or tribe, for example, though i'm the first to admit it has been ages since i last checked such things and the related experience spending mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T05:13:30-08:00","id":1498661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1498659#post1498659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK, there's not much in the way of limitations on learning Gifts, since in the end, they all spring from the teachings of spirits as a source.<br /> <br /> Should not be much harder than learning a gift not from one's auspice, breed or tribe, for example, though i'm the first to admit it has been ages since i last checked such things and the related experience spending mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm tempted to house-rule in an &quot;out of species&quot; EXP cost, such as 7x Gift Level, and that cost increase could be waived by being in an Ahadi, reducing it to 5x.<br /> <br /> But yeah interested to see if there's anything I've missed, or is buried in one of the 20th books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T05:40:18-08:00","id":1498663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1498661#post1498661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm tempted to house-rule in an &quot;out of species&quot; EXP cost, such as 7x Gift Level, and that cost increase could be waived by being in an Ahadi, reducing it to 5x.<br /> <br /> But yeah interested to see if there's anything I've missed, or is buried in one of the 20th books.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be overthinking things on the subject, if you don't mind me saying. As i said before, no matter the Fera Breed, the final source of teaching on the nature of Gifts, the manifold spirit choirs of the Umbra, is still the same.<br /> <br /> What's should be so different between learning certain gifts from a Swara or being taught by a jaggling of Cheetah (one of the basic teachers of Speed of Thought), for example?<br /> <br /> A lot of the gifts are already acessible by multiple sources anyway, so it ain't like immense imbalance issues would spring from just that. &quot;Gift from other breed/auspice/tribe&quot;, with maybe raising the specific gift's rank requirement one level or two if need be, should cover that base well enough, imho.<br /> <br /> Unless the Gift is something more obtuse and that hinges in concepts or qualities unique to a certain species of shapechanger, like Mokol\u00e9's Mnesis or a Garou trying to teach Step Sideways to most Bastet breeds (that don't have the inherent ability and learn it as a Gift instead). Then it's wholy up to whatever ST fiat one applies.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents of thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-03-2022, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T06:06:00-08:00","id":1498665,"title":"","content":"That's true, but there are some level 1 gifts which are insane if you divorce them from their context. Danger Sense, the Ratkin Gift, isn't dangerous in isolation. It's a very cool Gift for a Ratkin to start with, very thematic.<br /> <br /> When any Garou can learn it from a Rat Spirit for 5 EXP, things get a bit wonkier. Now for 5 EXP you have an infallible 3-60 second (depending on how long a turn is in the given scene) warning before danger arrives. Of course 5 EXP put into that Gift is 5 EXP you didn't put into another, but you see what I mean right - total cross-compatibility increases the number of possible combinations, and with each combination there's more potential for things to get a bit weird. I mean I can't see any evidence in W20 that a random Ragabash can learn the Gift, after all it isn't on any Garou list, they wouldn't know it exists, and even if they encountered the Gift's existence, I'm not sure the spirit world would be down with them having it - if they were, it would be on one of the many lists that are out there.<br /> <br /> Anyways main reason I came here was to find out whether W20 has anything official to say about a Bastet teaching a Garou, or a spirit teaching a Garou a Gift that isn't typically taught to Garou etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T07:53:43-08:00","id":1498677,"title":"","content":"My take:<br /> There were rules on this, iirc, in the revised Storyteller's Handbook. One should consider a Gift from another Fera-Breed to be one rank higher. Only Gifts up to rank 3 should be able to be learned and only if they do not require special anatomy of the changing breed to work.<br /> <br /> In general Gifts aren't limited to replicating Charms, so basically any ability imaginable could be available as Gift if one finds a spirit who reasonably could bestow this ability. Of course the ST should keep the whole thing balanced. But discovering Gifts, or rediscover them, is a source for Renown. And Gifts, even within a Rank, vary in their relative power or usefulness. 'Rage across the Heavens' has Gifts that are hard to come by, taught/bestowed by difficult to find spirits, but more powerful than other Gifts in the same level.<br /> <br /> Teaching Gift from Garou to Garou is regarded as wrong and rarely done, but possible, so Fera to Garou instruction would also be possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T08:06:06-08:00","id":1498679,"title":"","content":"Also, if a Gift relies on something that a Garou or Fera can do in their animal form that another breed can't do in theirs, usually due to anatomy, the Gift is a no-go. Sorry, Garou, but you can't shot web, and sorry, Ananasi, but you can't howl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T11:06:08-08:00","id":1498689,"title":"","content":"I believe theoretically most Gifts can be learned regardless if it is not normally available to that Fera. Meaning that the Gift is not impossible to learn or use. Gifts are actually more like a &quot;blessing&quot; bestowed upon one of the Fera, rather than a natural talent that can be improved or a skill to be learned. Even when a spirit is not the &quot;teacher&quot;, the other Fera is just telling them the secret of being able to use that blessing.<br /> <br /> If you think the Gift allows something that would be impossible for the person to do (it lacks the anatomy or whatever), then yeah feel free to disallow it. Don't do things that don't make sense to you.<br /> <br /> Mechanically it is just a matter of extra XP and assigning the appropriate level of the Gift. I know in earlier editions, Gifts could be learned at different levels based on the Fera, breed, auspice, tribe, etc. I think that has become more streamlined, at least among Garou so you don't have the same Gift at different ranks depending on breed, auspice, tribe in W20. But the Fera lists could still very well have different Gifts at different ranks - I haven't looked closely enough at the various Fera lists. If that is all you are looking for, the boost it by 1 extra XP beyond the normal &quot;out-of-breed/auspice/tribe, and decide what level of Gift it should be for that new breed.<br /> <br /> <br /> However, the issue has always been one of IC repercussions and how the ST wants to handle that. The books are very clear that the spirits are very angered if they are not the ones bestowing the Gifts. In Axis Mundi we're told that agreeing to not teach a Gift to anyone else is one of the basic chiminage agreements to learn Gifts in the first place, although the IC chiminage to learn Gifts is usually handwaved in practice in most games. But we can assume that 1) spirits don't want non-spirits making the decisions of who learns what Gifts, and 2) the standard practice of learning Gifts from spirits should always include a prohibition on teaching it to others. In other words, doing so should always be seen as a violation and crime against the spirits. It doesn't matter what the reason - the other person is part of your pack, you think it is essential to accomplish some important goal for Gaia, it's your best friend, etc. You are breaking an important oath. And that gets punished in the same way violating the laws of gravity punishes you. It's a bedrock law among the spirits. I would think teaching something out-of-Fera breed is probably even worse as there is ostensibly a reason why spirits do not normally teach that Gift to the other breed.<br /> <br /> But what does that mean in practice? This is where it gets harder as different STs run games very differently. But in broad measure I would recommend 1) the specific spirit who taught you that Gift becomes your enemy, 2) the person gets a lot of spirit notoriety in general, and 3) the buddies of the offended spirit (that spirit type or the entire spirit brood allied to it) is more offended. That is easy to say, but what are the consequences of that? IMO it should mean the spirits are less likely to teach spirits to that individual Fera (although I would say to be fair to players that they should still be able to learn their basic Gifts available to them, but perhaps with some delay in time, additional chiminage, or other inconvenience); that some spirits will actively complain to others about that individual even naming them and sometimes asking people to harass or punish them as part of a chiminage service they request of others; that spirits stop being friendly and won't answer questions, help that individual, etc. Each ST needs to figure out what is the right balance for their game in terms of preserving the setting, setting standards, but still keeping things fun for the players. Some STs will be very strict and others won't care at all about the roleplay. It's their game and their choice. I am not going to police it.<br /> <br /> Of course, such individuals do not need to be in the doghouse forever. There can always be quests and chiminage designed to assuage the anger of the spirits, repent, spiritually purify themselves, and restore the status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T13:08:56-08:00","id":1498697,"title":"","content":"It also seems important to point out something here:<br /> <br /> You need to know a Gift exists to ask a spirit to learn it. Garou don't get to read the gaming books, and know what's a Gift, what's a Background, what's a Merit, or whatever.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of the Garou have no idea what the unique Gifts of the Fera are to ask spirits to teach those Gifts to them.<br /> <br /> This is, inherently, the advantage of groups like the Beast Courts and the Ahadi: exposure to other changing breeds and more knowledge of what Gifts they know, which you could then try to learn yourself.<br /> <br /> Far before any mechanics need to come in to play, there is a basic rule for spending XP: You have to be able to explain how your character improved IC. If you can't explain how your PC obtained knowledge of a Gift to even start the process of learning that Gift, you can't buy it. That's an essential rule of character advancement in the game. Since most of the Fera are exceedingly guarded about sharing their unique Gifts, just don't make this easy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T09:37:20-08:00","id":1498770,"title":"","content":"I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> are on point as usual. There are some issues that we might want to raise in addition to that<ul><li>there are certain gifts that require users to have a very high rank (i.e. stepping sideways for Bastet) and for the duration of the setting they have not forced the spirits nor have they found a way to learn it early or nativley. The Bastet are well known for being sneaks and gift stealers, yet only Swara in the history of the breed managed to make it a low level gift</li> <li>Usually high level gifts are considered mysteries and secrets of the Tribes/Breeds and factions, and one would consider that this is for a reason</li> <li>Kitsune and Bastet have a special reputation for swiping magic, yet none of it has provoked conflict large enough to be a major thing, this would lead one to reinfoce the ideas that the gifts stolen are the simple ones rather than the Big Ones</li> <li>There had to be individuals with the level of wisdom, sneakery and cutthroatism that were willing to try this, but the setting implies that they either didn't or that they were few enough that this was not a replicable feat.</li> <li>There are Mokolo and Ananasi gifts that surely wouldn't work for non-lizards or non-spiders</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T09:48:59-08:00","id":1498772,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I completely overlooked that some Fera breeds can steal Gifts and they seem to get away with it. It could be that for some reason those breeds known for &quot;stealing&quot; Gifts somehow get an exception. The reason why might be unknown and a mystery in the setting, it might be because Gaia wants it that way, it might be because how their kind established a Pact it had actual exceptions, or some other reason that make sense. There might be no limits to those exceptions, or strong limits to those exceptions. Or maybe the spirits that teach the Bastet those Gifts don't mind it if spirits outside their brood get their Gifts stolen as long as their own Gifts are not stolen (this last one might require the ST to give some thought as to the spirits in the spirit brood tied to the Bastet). Or that certain Gifts can be stolen and others shouldn't be. Or some combination.<br /> <br /> If you are like me, you may spend entirely more time wondering about such things than the benefit it provides your game table. Or you might wing it entirely. It just depends on the nature of the ST and how many annoying questions the players at your game table like to ask. You can probably work out something that makes sense at your gaming table that is good enough for your needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T14:17:13-08:00","id":1498796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1498770#post1498770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kitsune and Bastet have a special reputation for swiping magic, yet none of it has provoked conflict large enough to be a major thing, this would lead one to reinfoce the ideas that the gifts stolen are the simple ones rather than the Big Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, at least, if any of them managed to swipe a &quot;big one&quot; Gift, they didn't let anyone know they did it.<br /> <br /> It seems pertinent to this line of thought to remember that not every breed learns Gifts the same way. The Bastet flip from how the Garou work. The Bastet, generally, don't learn their Gifts from spirits, and instead rely on exchanging them between each other, or learning them from others. Where the Garou have to go through rather significant training and potentially ordeals to learn a Gift from anyone that's not a spirit, but can learn from a spirit in a brief amount of time, the Bastet can learn to use Gifts in a day via getting them from other shifters.<br /> <br /> It can also be hard to &quot;swipe&quot; many potent Gifts, even for the Bastet or Kitsune, because without a teacher many Gifts don't get &quot;spammed&quot; in a fashion that makes them easy to study and internalize from stealth. Sitting around spying on a Den Parent explaining Gifts to Garou Cubs is only going to get you a lesson in low level Gifts. Watching a bunch of Garou combat is probably more than enough to figure out how Spirit of the Fray works because you're going to see it used a lot, while trying to observe a Ragabash in order to steal Open Seal is going to be a lot harder just because even if you do spy them using it, you only get a few seconds of &quot;study&quot; in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T06:50:59-08:00","id":1499214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1498697#post1498697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to know a Gift exists to ask a spirit to learn it. Garou don't get to read the gaming books, and know what's a Gift, what's a Background, what's a Merit, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div> and<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1498697#post1498697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vast majority of the Garou have no idea what the unique Gifts of the Fera are to ask spirits to teach those Gifts to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that doesn't make sense. Within the game world a Garou/Fera can imagine basically any power and then try to find a spirit that might be able to bestow this ability to her.<br /> Reading the game books, finding good equivalents for a power or simply rule, that a certain power is not available as Gift is the STs prerogative, of course. But finding new Gifts or lost ones is mentioned in the books as a source for Renown, for example. Obviously Gifts aren't a static set of powers that Gaia defined once to never change. I mean, computer-related Gifts can't have been around in the Dark Ages, or were they?<br /> <br /> And that is really big thing. I mean, we know of the Possession Charm as a means for Fomori creation, and those who have extended contacts with Vampires might also know of the Power of Dominate 5 or the Puppetry Arcanoi. These are powers mentioned around the campfire, when a visiting Galliard joins the caern guards for a cup of hot coffee. Still, never did a Fera, seemingly, find a spirit that bestows a Gift that granted a similar power. Doesn't mean that there couldn't be one. Authors might not have felt such a power is werewolf-like, and I agree. But a player might feel that such a power would very well complement with his characters nature and modus operandi, and therefore try to find it....<br /> <br /> If your ST gives the guideline that only Gifts printed in official WtA books are permitted, then really, reading though these should be a fair approach. Because the powers are probably powers the character would imagine anyway and possibly try to find a spirit to bestow that power.<br /> <br /> So, sure, the Ahadi and Beast Courts have more exposure to Gifts from other Fera, but really imagination and exposure to fantasy films, tv shows or comic books might be enough to get ideas for what powers would be a nice Gift, and from there the journey to find a spirits starts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1498697#post1498697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Far before any mechanics need to come in to play, there is a basic rule for spending XP: You have to be able to explain how your character improved IC. If you can't explain how your PC obtained knowledge of a Gift to even start the process of learning that Gift, you can't buy it. That's an essential rule of character advancement in the game. Since most of the Fera are exceedingly guarded about sharing their unique Gifts, just don't make this easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree on foundation of the reasoning above.<br /> XP, as a game mechanic, are OOC. Becoming a Gift bestowed on yourself isn't even an effort on the garou's side. Finding the spirit and convincing it, is - maybe. I mean, there are &quot;other approaches to learning Gifts&quot; in Axis Mundi, for troupes who find them more to their liking.<br /> XP are a means of balancing the characters, and they aren't the best approach, just one that was common, when the game was released. I mean, Chronicles of Darkness &quot;Beats&quot; are another means. WoD has never had a system for learning curves and training anyway. Unless you use the rules given with the Instruction secondary skill. Basically, you &quot;should&quot; explain why your character raised Strength, Appearance or Gnosis, but the mechanics clearly state, that participation in enough game sessions and story ends gets you XP to spend on such raises. And you also have to buy Gifts.<br /> <br /> Does it make sense? No. I mean:<br /> &quot;Can you bestow the Gift on me, that allows me to heal the wounds of others?&quot;<br /> &quot;No, young garou, for reasons I can't explain within the constrains of these world, you have to wait for an arbitrary moment, not governed within the logic of this world, before I have the ability.&quot;<br /> &quot;So, in the beginning of the next games session then?&quot;<br /> &quot;Sure.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 12-09-2022, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T08:27:58-08:00","id":1499223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499214#post1499214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, that doesn't make sense. Within the game world a Garou/Fera can imagine basically any power and then try to find a spirit that might be able to bestow this ability to her.<br /> Reading the game books, finding good equivalents for a power or simply rule, that a certain power is not available as Gift is the STs prerogative, of course. But finding new Gifts or lost ones is mentioned in the books as a source for Renown, for example. Obviously Gifts aren't a static set of powers that Gaia defined once to never change. I mean, computer-related Gifts can't have been around in the Dark Ages, or were they?<br /> <br /> And that is really big thing. I mean, we know of the Possession Charm as a means for Fomori creation, and those who have extended contacts with Vampires might also know of the Power of Dominate 5 or the Puppetry Arcanoi. These are powers mentioned around the campfire, when a visiting Galliard joins the caern guards for a cup of hot coffee. Still, never did a Fera, seemingly, find a spirit that bestows a Gift that granted a similar power. Doesn't mean that there couldn't be one. Authors might not have felt such a power is werewolf-like, and I agree. But a player might feel that such a power would very well complement with his characters nature and modus operandi, and therefore try to find it....</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see it. Gifts (or other splat powers for that matter) are not a list that's perceptible in game. They can be a matter of tales and stories, but you would still need the idea of the gift and the right spirit to ask and convince to teach you if that gift it even possible. It's fully in the ST's purview how common or rare gifts are, but nothing in the game lore points to there being a hollistic study of how powers work and where you can learn them. You learn them by seeing them from others or asking advice from elders by default. Going into the Umbra to develop a new gift is a feat worth of a whole story and not something that should be undertaken lightly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499214#post1499214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it make sense? No. I mean:<br /> &quot;Can you bestow the Gift on me, that allows me to heal the wounds of others?&quot;<br /> &quot;No, young garou, for reasons I can't explain within the constrains of these world, you have to wait for an arbitrary moment, not governed within the logic of this world, before I have the ability.&quot;<br /> &quot;So, in the beginning of the next games session then?&quot;<br /> &quot;Sure.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not how gifts or experience work. IC or OOC. You decide what you want to buy, ask the storyteller if it's justified and have the scene of seeking out the spirit and actually learning it. The act of learnign a spirit is agreed on OOC, but learning it and actually interacting with the spirit is fully IC.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T14:11:48-08:00","id":1499244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499214#post1499214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where, exactly, do you show that the line of reasoning doesn't make sense? You can disagree with it, but I'd like you to justify this a bit more strongly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Within the game world a Garou/Fera can imagine basically any power and then try to find a spirit that might be able to bestow this ability to her. </div> </div> </div>OK. So are you going to force players to buy Gifts they don't want because they pick the wrong spirits or the spirits interpret their vague requests differently than the Gift the player really wants?<br /> <br /> The OP mentions the Danger Sense Gift. If the Garou doesn't know the exact nature of the Gift, and the right spirits to ask, should the ST rule they end up getting the Heightened Senses Gift instead because that's what the spirit they asked would teach a Garou that wants to be better equipped to sense danger approaching them?<br /> <br /> Let's also not forget context here like the Firebringer Gift. It's a Rank 6 Gift for a Ragabash to turn another supernatural's power into a Gift, which they can't use themselves, they can only pass that on to others. And they have to get hit with said power as well.&quot;In theory&quot; arguments where things are technical possible doesn't address how easy or likely something is to happen. As noted finding a new or lost Gift is Renown worthy because it's special. It's work and effort that a character has to put in, not something for players to get because they read about a Gift in a Fera supplement and decide they know how to ask the spirits for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, computer-related Gifts can't have been around in the Dark Ages, or were they? </div> </div> </div>Considering there's an entire Tribe of Garou that are dedicated to trying to figure out new Gifts to learn as technology spirits evolve as technology changes, and they've managed to work out less than a dozen Gifts from that process in the last half century, I again point out that &quot;possible&quot; does not mean,&quot; easy&quot; or &quot;likely.&quot;<br /> <br /> You seem to be under the assumption I said, &quot;the PC needs knowledge to get a Gift,&quot; as meaning, &quot;the PCs can never acquire that knowledge.&quot; I didn't. I said make getting that knowledge appropriately difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But a player might feel that such a power would very well complement with his characters nature and modus operandi, and therefore try to find it.... </div> </div> </div>And? Let them try. Making it easy ruins the whole point. These sorts of things are supposed to be a challenge (or not, there are a bunch of pretty potent mind-control Gifts in the Garou lists, it might not be a neat package like Dominate but it's not like there's nothing there at all).<br /> <br /> The ST's job is just to make sure it's clear to the player how hard that task is going to be in their game so the player is on the same page as them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, sure, the Ahadi and Beast Courts have more exposure to Gifts from other Fera, but really imagination and exposure to fantasy films, tv shows or comic books might be enough to get ideas for what powers would be a nice Gift, and from there the journey to find a spirits starts. </div> </div> </div>How much free time do your PCs have? How is their pack, Sept, family, and Tribe, going to feel about them going, &quot;Hey folks, I saw this neat thing on TV, so I'm going on a months long quest into the Umbra to see if I can find a spirit that knows a Gift that will teach it to me even though I could just learn a well known Gift that's 95% the same thing!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I disagree on foundation of the reasoning above. </div> </div> </div>You... disagree with the idea that PCs should have an IC rationale for how they learned something? Would you let a Garou that's never held an external weapon in their life buy Melee? Or would you make them justify it via training and instruction?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, Chronicles of Darkness &quot;Beats&quot; are another means. </div> </div> </div>Beats are literally just XP with more player agency in when they get awarded instead of ST fiat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WoD has never had a system for learning curves and training anyway. </div> </div> </div>And? I'm not talking about that. I'm just saying that players need to explain the IC methods of how their character learned something before they get to spend XP on it. Something that applies to all traits, not just Gifts. Hell it even applies to things like Backgrounds, Renown, and Rank, and you don't spend XP on those.<br /> <br /> Sheet improvements come from IC actions (even if downtime or off-screen ones). The OOC mechanics mediating how frequently/rapidly you can get them is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it make sense? No. I mean: </div> </div> </div>If you want to have a thread about how to handle the inconsistencies of the WoD XP system and in-game actions that would justify new traits even though you don't have the XP for them at the moment, feel free to start one. That's not the point at hand here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T05:38:57-08:00","id":1499431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499244#post1499244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where, exactly, do you show that the line of reasoning doesn't make sense? You can disagree with it, but I'd like you to justify this a bit more strongly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I understood the passages I quoted read like Garou would have very little knowledge on what Gifts exist or what powers are backgrounds, Gifts, fetishes etc, because they can't read rule books. I find that this doesn't fit with the oral tradition and education Garou should be subjected to, if living in septs and participating in sept/tribal traditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499244#post1499244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. So are you going to force players to buy Gifts they don't want because they pick the wrong spirits or the spirits interpret their vague requests differently than the Gift the player really wants?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't you?<br /> Hey, the rules state, a fox spirit can teach you '<i>Obscure the Truth'</i> but the spirit can also tell you it did and you wouldn't know...<br /> <br /> But, kidding aside, I'm not that dicki-sh that I would force players to buy Gifts, because of a 'wrong spirit' or 'vague request'. In any case W20 removed all chance for misunderstanding from 'Spirit Speech'. And Axis Mundi doesn't specify specific Gifts in a sprits 'Gift Lore' entry, but only keywords regarding the theme of Gifts the spirit might bestow on characters. So, 'vague request' or 'wrong spirit' are somewhat unlikely scenarios. Your example following not withstanding, or course.<br /> <br /> But, I also had NPCs like Mentors or pack totems recommend or even force PCs to learn a Gift they deemed suitable or necessary for the character. Often that were Gifts that players hadn't known about, since they were from more obscure books, like Dark Ages or something. I can't remember any player objecting there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499244#post1499244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OP mentions the Danger Sense Gift. If the Garou doesn't know the exact nature of the Gift, and the right spirits to ask, should the ST rule they end up getting the Heightened Senses Gift instead because that's what the spirit they asked would teach a Garou that wants to be better equipped to sense danger approaching them?</div> </div> </div> </div>True, that could happen. But as ST I have the ability to communicate with the player OOC in parallel to the scene developing. So, if I wasn't sure what Gift the player was aiming for, I'd simply ask. After all it is a collaborative game to some extend. If there are obstacles the PCs can't overcome because of OOC reasons, like me not wanting the character to have a specific Gift (at this point or ever), I'd communicate that OOC. Just like I would tell players that they can enter Maleas with their Fostern pack, but every character will die or become otherwise unplayable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499244#post1499244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's also not forget context here like the Firebringer Gift. It's a Rank 6 Gift for a Ragabash to turn another supernatural's power into a Gift, which they can't use themselves, they can only pass that on to others. And they have to get hit with said power as well.&quot;In theory&quot; arguments where things are technical possible doesn't address how easy or likely something is to happen. As noted finding a new or lost Gift is Renown worthy because it's special. It's work and effort that a character has to put in, not something for players to get because they read about a Gift in a Fera supplement and decide they know how to ask the spirits for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is worth 7 Wisdom to find a new Gift in W20. That is the same as finding three mates and procreate thrice. Teaching other Garou is worth 3 to 5, depending of field of study. So, it is kind of difficult the set things into relation here. But that is true with most Renown table entries, since they are short statements without context.<br /> <br /> In any case, I would think Garou finding completely new Gifts or rediscover forgotten ones happens rarely, since most tribes tend to teach knowledge of Gifts already known to their members and most are good with the options they have (and possibly live with the knowledge that going beyond these choices might be untraditional).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499244#post1499244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering there's an entire Tribe of Garou that are dedicated to trying to figure out new Gifts to learn as technology spirits evolve as technology changes, and they've managed to work out less than a dozen Gifts from that process in the last half century, I again point out that &quot;possible&quot; does not mean,&quot; easy&quot; or &quot;likely.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Although it can be up the the ST if he believes the Gifts printed are the only ones in existence. Or, if opening the game up to more possibilities. I mean, since the Storyteller's Vault is up, you don't even have to come up with Gifts yourself any more...<br /> <br /> It is maybe to sub-par editing on White Wolf's side that there are some Gifts that are vaguely identical to others, and some that have a similar theme but different mechanics - for authors seemingly didn't know that they were creating duplicates. Meanwhile there is a word count for books and I'm sure, there were plenty of more ideas for Gifts that could have made it to print...<br /> <br /> For balancing reasons, I usually only allow Gifts that are printed in my game's though. But that is an &quot;a can of worms once opened&quot;-problem. For a small troupe I could course-correct if a home-brewed Gift was turning out to be chronicle breaking. For a 20+ players LARP chronicle I can't do so easily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499244#post1499244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be under the assumption I said, &quot;the PC needs knowledge to get a Gift,&quot; as meaning, &quot;the PCs can never acquire that knowledge.&quot; I didn't. I said make getting that knowledge appropriately difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly I misinterpreted your statement. I, too, think that it should be possible, but not too easy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499244#post1499244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And? Let them try. Making it easy ruins the whole point. These sorts of things are supposed to be a challenge (or not, there are a bunch of pretty potent mind-control Gifts in the Garou lists, it might not be a neat package like Dominate but it's not like there's nothing there at all).<br /> <br /> The ST's job is just to make sure it's clear to the player how hard that task is going to be in their game so the player is on the same page as them.<br /> <br /> How much free time do your PCs have? How is their pack, Sept, family, and Tribe, going to feel about them going, &quot;Hey folks, I saw this neat thing on TV, so I'm going on a months long quest into the Umbra to see if I can find a spirit that knows a Gift that will teach it to me even though I could just learn a well known Gift that's 95% the same thing!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was more like this:<br /> <br /> It is easy to find a reason why a Garou would find inspiration for power to desire - be it Galliard tales or modern media. It is a bit trickier to think of a spirit who might have a power like this on the 'Gift Lore' entry (assuming all spirits have this, not just the one's specifically printed in Axis Mundi). From there it is either to find the spirit in the Umbra, find paraphernalia to help in a summoning or outright summon a spirit, Call of Duty if a spirit name is known. And from there the negotiations with the spirit start. And the result can be that the Gift is leaned that is identical to a Gift commonly found by another Fera.<br /> <br /> One doesn't need to be a member of the Ahadi or the Beast Courts for that. If one is, then one is even more exposed to tales of the powers of the other Fera, but it isn't a pre-requisite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499244#post1499244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You... disagree with the idea that PCs should have an IC rationale for how they learned something? Would you let a Garou that's never held an external weapon in their life buy Melee? Or would you make them justify it via training and instruction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. I could rationalise that a PC used mental attributes and therefore is allowed to increase them with XP. I'm not tracking if the player ever rolled any dice pool with mental attributes. Does the player have to say &quot;my character is sitting down to solve sodokus&quot; at least thrice to allow the increase. Is plastic surgery required for Appearance increases (thank god V5 got rid of that trait)? Is Charisma increased by training or would training in these field not raise Expression, Leadership or Subterfuge instead?<br /> How much devotion has a PC to show to increase Totem? How does a character show how in-tune with the world one is to raise Gnosis?<br /> <br /> Players usually have a rationale for why they want to increase a trait and there is often an easy way to find an IC rationale as well. I encourage players to write down a few sentences on why they think their character's traits should be increased (especially since for the LARP game, this runs through a web interface), so their personal character development is a bit fleshed out.<br /> <br /> And, we have a system in place to prohibit rapid increase in stats, so once you raised a stat, you have to use the new stat for a couple of games, until you can raise it again. In a tabletop game a ST would discuss this with the players but for fairness' sake and a collaborative play that isn't working in LARP. Also, we use the games that happen to measure, not the real world time to easily adjust for games that have to be rescheduled or canceled.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if we would use the Instruction skills rules from PGttG, the times to increase a stat would drastically change, and be partially up to luck (dice rolls). That might overall be a more accurate simulation of the real world, but then again, it is a role playing game not a simulation.<br /> <br /> So, I can totally understand that STs and players want an IC rationale for what the character learns or raises, but also totally understands if that is rather abstract or hand waived, too. It doesn't always contribute to the story or the game flow if the IC rationale is discussed in detail. Again, Gifts are probably something I would discuss in more detain, unless the group and I agreed on one of the alternative approaches to Gift learning as detailed in Axis Mundi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499244#post1499244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beats are literally just XP with more player agency in when they get awarded instead of ST fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but that can make a difference in the feeling of how to are spend, too. MtAw had a passage that players could have their characters perform relatively simple tasks that they make a bit harder by adding conditions and therefore earn beats. And the rules state that this is okay, that is what training is. You make things harder for you to hone your skills. The WoD XP don't work that way.<br /> <br /> Personally, I found RuneQuest's approach rather nice. It had occasionally random increases in stats (due to rolling botches), but also had downtime with a specific number of hours of training and the players could award these to the skills they are trying to increase. The increases were not automatic, especially if the skill was already at a high level. Therefore the characters didn't increase in their abilities in a comparable way, but if the troupe is okay with that, why not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499244#post1499244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And? I'm not talking about that. I'm just saying that players need to explain the IC methods of how their character learned something before they get to spend XP on it. Something that applies to all traits, not just Gifts. Hell it even applies to things like Backgrounds, Renown, and Rank, and you don't spend XP on those.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I say, if the ST and players all are fine with one characters raise of medicine two to medicine three they don't need to detail the IC methods.<br /> If the raise is trivial, that is.<br /> <br /> There, for example, is no need to define if the part of the story three sessions ago, when the character did a lot of mundane first aid is a suitable reason to increase the trait now (since there weren't XP around then, but now are), or if there is need to get instructions from an authority or if autodidaction can be a thing for Medicine or if using &quot;Mother's Touch&quot; often is a reason, even when it is now (in W20) rolled against Empathy, rather than Medicine. Or even if the character needs to study for a month then have the instructor roll Manipulation + Instruction against 10 minus the characters Intelligence. If only 3 successes were scored, the character has to study another month, for the last remaining success to allow to spend 4XP. Because that is what the PGttG states.<br /> <br /> Why go through this, if in everyone's head the increase is okay and doesn't need a specific IC reasoning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T05:53:47-08:00","id":1499432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499223#post1499223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see it. Gifts (or other splat powers for that matter) are not a list that's perceptible in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally. Databases compiled by Glass Walkers not withstanding <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499223#post1499223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can be a matter of tales and stories, but you would still need the idea of the gift and the right spirit to ask and convince to teach you if that gift it even possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>The right spirit is who exactly? It is not that there is one spirit that teaches a specific gift. Spirit types have their &quot;Gift lore&quot; which details the themes the Gifts have that specific spirits of these types could possibly teach/bestow. Sure, any individual spirit might have the ability or not. Still, to find/summon a darkness spirit and ask for the Gift &quot;Shroud&quot; to be bestowed is a no-brainer. The Gifts spirits can bestow correspond with they natures and types and therefore it is possible to deduct where to start looking for power as a Gift. If the spirits can't bestow the Gift, one possibly gains information on how to proceed, if a ST wants to create a larger story around the matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499223#post1499223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fully in the ST's purview how common or rare gifts are, but nothing in the game lore points to there being a hollistic study of how powers work and where you can learn them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are references to the fact that you probably get the oral lore which Gifts there are available to you from you elders, and that you have to visit a Caern of the level equal to the Gifts rank to find a spirit that can bestow this Gift. That is, despite the Caern levels possibly being a OOC trait.<br /> <br /> But again, the basic idea to ask a spirit that shows similar characteristics than the power I want to have for a thematically corresponding Gift is not something that only the wisest of Thurges come up with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499223#post1499223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You learn them by seeing them from others or asking advice from elders by default. Going into the Umbra to develop a new gift is a feat worth of a whole story and not something that should be undertaken lightly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. That is how it should be.<br /> <br /> Although a spirit patron simply granting a new power, because the ST wants to, is also fair.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T06:12:05-08:00","id":1499433,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;I misunderstood you,&quot; bit gets old fast considering how much of your next post ignores me saying, &quot;Sheet improvements come from IC actions <b>(even if downtime or off-screen ones)</b>. The OOC mechanics mediating how frequently/rapidly you can get them is irrelevant.&quot; Emphasized the important part for you.<br /> <br /> There isn't even a point to responding to most of your post. Even when there's a hint of a point, there's no willingness to address the obvious context issues with things characters could do; but generally don't because it would require a lot of people being dumb at once.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T13:00:51-08:00","id":1499466,"title":"","content":"Maybe the issues in the given context aren't so obvious to me as they seem to be to you.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And thanks for the emphasis on the important part. I got that. I just feel that there isn't even a need for that. For, if it is &quot;off-screen&quot; then the ST and the player don't even have to be on the same page what &quot;IC action&quot; warranted, for example, the raise in medicine knowledge. The ST might remember the character succeeding in rolls that saved another PC, while the player might think of his character helping in a local clinic in the downtime.<br /> If the exchange goes: &quot;Can I raise medicine to three?&quot; - &quot;Sure&quot; then that is okay, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 12-12-2022, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T15:02:20-08:00","id":1499474,"title":"","content":"Off screen does not mean not discussed. It means it didn't warrant enough importance to come up at the table. <br /> <br /> On screen: Stuff that happens at the table during scenes.<br /> Downtime: Stuff that happens at the table, but outside of the focus of specific scenes.<br /> Off screen: Stuff that doesn't happen at the table, but still happens in the narrative.<br /> <br /> An off screen XP chat is:<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, this current story has left my PC with plenty of time to work on his clinic, would it be cool to raise [Trait] even though it didn't come up last session?&quot;<br /> &quot;Yeah, that's cool.&quot;<br /> &quot;Thanks.&quot;<br /> <br /> Notice that the player and ST are still on the same page, and if not there is room to make sure they can get there.<br /> <br /> What are you even trying to get at here? I have no idea what point you're really trying to make in all this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T22:34:22-08:00","id":1499496,"title":"","content":"I get what your point is. My point would be, that for some trait increases the dialogue can be as short as:<br /> Player: &quot;Can I raise medicine to three?&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;Sure&quot;<br /> <br /> If player and ST agree on the new trait being adequate for the character at that point there is no deed to define what &quot;IC action&quot; or sum of those lead to the rationale that the trait may be raised. The understanding that the new trait is suitable for the character at this point in the story, based on the sum of all actions in the story so far, is enough.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T23:53:30-08:00","id":1499503,"title":"","content":"In general, that's not really contrary to what I'm saying. The IC actions predicating the trait raise is still there, even if the ST and player don't have to discuss it explicitly. I have no idea why you think I'd have a problem with the ST and player just agreeing without needing to enumerate the reasons why to increase most traits.<br /> <br /> Gifts (and a number of other WtA specific traits like Renown, Rank, Totem, Rites, etc.) are something I would argue requires a bit more, because they have more rules about how their gained. These things are elaborated on in the books. Gifts aren't like Medicine where they can just go up as a representation of accumulated life experiences. Until you meet the specific criteria laid out by the books for your shifter breed to learn a Gift, you can't get it. A Garou can't just learn a Gift turning a road trip back to their Sept that serves as the transition point between game-time units. A Garou has to address chiminage to the spirit in some fashion.<br /> <br /> This doesn't have to be a big deal if the ST and player are in agreement that the Gift is one the Garou should have easy access too (Sept of appropriate Rank, access to Garou skilled with spirits to handle certain things, being in good standing with the Sept, etc.), and the chiminage can just be a point of Gnosis, but that needs to be established so the point of Gnosis gets marked off the sheet, or the favor promised to the spirit is noted in case it doesn't get finished and the Garou has to mend that, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T04:41:17-08:00","id":1499510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499503#post1499503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, that's not really contrary to what I'm saying. The IC actions predicating the trait raise is still there, even if the ST and player don't have to discuss it explicitly. I have no idea why you think I'd have a problem with the ST and player just agreeing without needing to enumerate the reasons why to increase most traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it is not contrary to what you are saying, it is supplementary. And I didn't think you would have a problem with it. I thought I didn't manage to convey to you what I wanted to express.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499503#post1499503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gifts (and a number of other WtA specific traits like Renown, Rank, Totem, Rites, etc.) are something I would argue requires a bit more, because they have more rules about how their gained. These things are elaborated on in the books. Gifts aren't like Medicine where they can just go up as a representation of accumulated life experiences. Until you meet the specific criteria laid out by the books for your shifter breed to learn a Gift, you can't get it. A Garou can't just learn a Gift turning a road trip back to their Sept that serves as the transition point between game-time units. A Garou has to address chiminage to the spirit in some fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I laughed when I read that, because in our LARP game there is recurring joke that once a character was asked if he was able to use the 'Gremlins' and he replied &quot;No&quot;. Being the only Adren in the sept at that time and the other PCs plans of attacking a fomori hideout depending in the Gift he was asked if he could learn the Gift on route to the fomori hideout.<br /> <br /> But of course you are right, for a lot of traits and Gifts specifically there, there are IC things happening to acquire them.<br /> <br /> That is, unless the ST reduces or completely drops these requirements, as proposed alternative play style in the aforementioned sidebar on page 37 of Axis Mundi. But I never met a group that played that way, although I often played with groups that used the Downtime to learn Gifts.<br /> The paragraph even states that Werewolf would loose parts of its mystical qualities if these aspect was removed, and that is true, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499503#post1499503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't have to be a big deal if the ST and player are in agreement that the Gift is one the Garou should have easy access too (Sept of appropriate Rank, access to Garou skilled with spirits to handle certain things, being in good standing with the Sept, etc.), and the chiminage can just be a point of Gnosis, but that needs to be established so the point of Gnosis gets marked off the sheet, or the favor promised to the spirit is noted in case it doesn't get finished and the Garou has to mend that, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree.<br /> <br /> Except for the chiminage part, because re-reading that section of Axis Mundi I came across these sentences:<br /> <i>Spirit-teachers often do not accept chiminage. If the werewolf agrees to revere his teacher and follow through with his learning, the teacher will be satisfied. The process of instruction offers many opportunities for the Garou to obey his teacher\u2019s requests.</i><br /> <br /> For the general discussion about Gifts not of the Breed, Auspice, Tribe, or Changing Breed, it is worth noting that Axis Mundi also re-confirms that the Garou who are bestowed Gifts usually have to maintain secrecy about the Gifts. That certainly includes not teaching other Garou, Fera or even Kin, but might be understood as to also not publicly announcing what Gifts a Garou possesses or who the spirit-teacher was or other aspects of the Gifts and it's powers.<br /> <br /> So, this leads me to believe that Garou would be more likely to say stuff like &quot;I have a greater tolerance for toxins, I should be with the group attacking the fomori with the suspected venom powers&quot; as opposed to &quot;I'll go for the the toxin fomori, for I have 'Resist Toxin'.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sure, the Elders will, in accordance with the paragraph in Axis Mundi, help younger Garou to get Gifts, pointing them to the appropriate spirit-teachers and such, but entrusting a secret to a worthy person is also a way of honourably handling that secret...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T12:54:39-08:00","id":1499564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499510#post1499510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But of course you are right, for a lot of traits and Gifts specifically there, there are IC things happening to acquire them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I continue to be confused as to the point you're trying to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ,,,Axis Mundi. </div> </div> </div>OK. Can we stop treating a 2e book as the one and only book that counts in this discussion? While the short section you keep referencing isn't bad or anything, there's a few parts of it that weren't continued into the Rev. and W20 books (namely the idea that the Garou have a strong bond with spirit mentors that turns into a reward in and of itself for the spirit that justifies not coming to the spirit with chiminage as the default).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirit-teachers often do not accept chiminage. If the werewolf agrees to revere his teacher and follow through with his learning, the teacher will be satisfied. The process of instruction offers many opportunities for the Garou to obey his teacher\u2019s requests. </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing either, you actually play that out, and this thing I said still applies, &quot;the favor promised to the spirit is noted in case it doesn't get finished and the Garou has to mend that,&quot; or you don't establish what the Garou has done, IC, to justify the spirit's favor. Even if you want to hold to the 2e Axis Mundi approach to things, it's an every strong reason not to hand-wave Gift learning because 2e implies a much more involved process that has ramifications for later events that need to be established.<br /> <br /> Yes, there are optional rules in the books for people that want to play around with the base assumptions. But the base assumptions don't change because we can change them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T01:38:03-08:00","id":1499623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499564#post1499564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I continue to be confused as to the point you're trying to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>That there could be cases where, most likely for traits other than Gifts, where the ST and player agree on the new state of the character (trait raised, Gift learned, etc.) but agree on ignoring the IC actions usually needed to warrant such an increase.<br /> It's not<br /> &quot;This specific thing that warranted the XP expenditure happened off-screen, let's move on.&quot;<br /> It is<br /> &quot;Something undefined happened off-screen that warranted the XP expenditure, let's move on.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499564#post1499564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. Can we stop treating a 2e book as the one and only book that counts in this discussion? While the short section you keep referencing isn't bad or anything, there's a few parts of it that weren't continued into the Rev. and W20 books (namely the idea that the Garou have a strong bond with spirit mentors that turns into a reward in and of itself for the spirit that justifies not coming to the spirit with chiminage as the default).<br /> <br /> Here's the thing either, you actually play that out, and this thing I said still applies, &quot;the favor promised to the spirit is noted in case it doesn't get finished and the Garou has to mend that,&quot; or you don't establish what the Garou has done, IC, to justify the spirit's favor. Even if you want to hold to the 2e Axis Mundi approach to things, it's an every strong reason not to hand-wave Gift learning because 2e implies a much more involved process that has ramifications for later events that need to be established.<br /> <br /> Yes, there are optional rules in the books for people that want to play around with the base assumptions. But the base assumptions don't change because we can change them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct, an I wouldn't encourage STs to hand-wave Gift learning in most cases. It is, or should be, an element that adds to your character.<br /> <br /> However, I can see (and have played as guest in troupes) that handle it differently. They were very focused on the general story line, the main plot so to speak, and personal character development (in a sense that the characters became more layered) were also almost exclusively driven by the plot the ST provided as main story.<br /> It is like D&amp;D can be more of a strategy game and less of an RPG, if you solely focus on dungeon crawls and all interaction is with hostile NPCs.<br /> <br /> So, part of my point is, there are this alternate play-styles that work for people and they are not necessarily how the designers/authors of WtA intended the game to be used, but they are imo valid approaches, too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T02:04:31-08:00","id":1499625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498657-teaching-gifts-between-breeds?p=1499623#post1499623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That there could be cases where, most likely for traits other than Gifts, where the ST and player agree on the new state of the character (trait raised, Gift learned, etc.) but agree on ignoring the IC actions usually needed to warrant such an increase.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, part of my point is, there are this alternate play-styles that work for people and they are not necessarily how the designers/authors of WtA intended the game to be used, but they are imo valid approaches, too. </div> </div> </div>So, troupes can use the Golden Rule. Great. I didn't need to be told that, nor does it really address the question the thread was started to address. I'm not declaring playstyles that take large liberties with the default game invalid. I've been trying to address what the actual default of the game is, since the OP asked how to handle something and didn't indicate they're looking for an answer of, &quot;just house rule it to whatever you want.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}